---
layout: layouts/opengraph.liquid
eleventyImport:
  collections: ["post"]
pagination:
  data: "collections.post"
  size: 1
  alias: "entry"
permalink: "/opengraph{{ entry.url }}"
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{% comment %}
Task 20. One OG card page per post (spec §A.1/§F.4), adapted to this
theme's content/ input dir. Source paginates `collections.posts` with
permalink "/opengraph{{ post.url }}" against a project-root input dir; this
theme's six post-type directories already give output-relative permalinks
(content/{articles,notes,bookmarks,likes,replies,photos}/<slug>.11tydata.js
—> "/articles/<slug>/" etc.), and permalinks are output-relative regardless
of dir.input (spec §F.1), so the identical "/opengraph" + own-permalink
pattern transfers unchanged: "/opengraph/articles/<slug>/",
"/opengraph/notes/<slug>/", and so on for all six.

collections.post is every post-type fixture tagged "post" (see each
<type>.11tydata.js) — this page set is deliberately NOT added to that
collection itself (eleventyExcludeFromCollections above), so it can never
recursively include itself, and so it stays out of the Atom feed
(eleventy.config.js's feedPlugin reads collection "post") and the
homepage's h-feed (content/index.liquid loops collections.post) without
depending on this template simply lacking a `tags: post` key — that
absence alone would already work, but the explicit flag makes the exclusion
a deliberate property of this file rather than an accident of what its
front matter happens to omit (plan Task 20 step 5).

Pagefind: the built output lands under /opengraph/<type>/<slug>/, outside
every one of the six directories package.json's search-index script scopes
its --glob to. That glob is already an allow-list of exactly the six
post-type output directories (not this one), so it already excludes this
page set with no changes needed — verified in test/build.mjs's "pagefind
indexes only content pages" check, extended in this task to assert
/opengraph/ specifically never appears in the indexed set.

Gated to build mode only (eleventy.config.js: OG_CARD_TEMPLATE ignore) —
this theme's existing ELEVENTY_RUN_MODE idiom (see that file and
_11ty/imagePlugin.js), not a second custom env var like source's
PRODUCTION_BUILD (spec §A.5's intent, this repo's own idiom for the gate).

Photo posts still get a card here for archive consistency (spec §F.6) even
though og:image (_11ty/imagePlugin.js's ogImageSource) never points at it
for that type — the photo itself is always the better, more honest preview,
and needs no screenshot service at all.

The 60-day/git-created-timestamp freshness check the port source runs before
returning a screenshot URL (imagePlugin.js:211-222, returning "" for a post
too new to have a git-committed timestamp yet) is deliberately NOT ported:
its premise doesn't hold here. This build renders the post page AND its OG
card in the same Eleventy pass, so by the time ogImageSource emits a URL
for a given post, /opengraph<that post's permalink> has already been
written to _site in this exact build — there is no staged-deploy race for
it to guard against, and Indiekit's file-system store gives no general
guarantee of a git-committed timestamp to key that check on regardless
(spec §E.11). og:image is designed to never return "" instead (see
ogImageSource's own comment) — an empty content attribute is worse than
omitting the tag, and omitting the tag isn't available here since base.liquid
always emits one.
{% endcomment %}
